{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1569351691,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0OTc4Njg2MDM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3706","origin":"github"},"title":"known_failure_v6_or_later is in effect only when version forced via global datalad.repo.version","message":"In the light of #3648 and while troubleshooting https://github.com/datalad/datalad-crawler/issues/55 I saw that the test marked as `@known_failure_v6_or_later` was not skipped although default version for the repositories now should be 7... and looking at the code the reason is obvious:\n```python\ndef known_failure_v6_or_later(func):\n    \"\"\"Test decorator marking a test as known to fail in a v6+ test run\n\n    If datalad.repo.version is set to 6 or later behaves like `known_failure`.\n    Otherwise the original (undecorated) function is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    from datalad import cfg\n\n    version = cfg.obtain(\"datalad.repo.version\")\n    if version and version \u003e= 6:\n\n        @known_failure\n        @wraps(func)\n        @attr('known_failure_v6_or_later')\n        @attr('v6_or_later')\n        def v6_func(*args, **kwargs):\n            return func(*args, **kwargs)\n\n        return v6_func\n\n    return func\n```\n\nso we would skip only when we force default repo version to be \u003e= 6, so with annex having v7 as default we wouldn't skip those (for better or for worse).\n\nI am not sure yet if we should treat it as a bug (and fix it by eg considering also a version of annex) or a feature (that actually virtually no tests blew up) and start deprecating this decorator ;)","files":null}]}